.TH PULLOUT 1 "September 2026" "pullout 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pullout \- pull a regex-delimited substring out of a stream, by context

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pullout
[\-A | \-a] [\-d] [\-m]
.I bmatch want
[\fIamatch\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pullout
reads a program's output on standard input and, for each match of
.RI ' bmatch ... want ... amatch '
prints the text that matched
.IR want .
.IR bmatch ", " want " and " amatch
are all regular expressions; matching is always case-insensitive.

By default a lazy ".*?" gap is inserted between
.IR bmatch " and " want ,
and between
.IR want " and " amatch ,
so the three arguments need not be adjacent in the input. Use \-d to require them to be adjacent instead.

Without \-m, each input line is matched independently: all of
.IR bmatch ", " want " and " amatch
must appear on that one line, and only the first match per line is used. With \-m, the whole input is read
at once, "." is allowed to match a newline, and every non-overlapping match anywhere in the input is
reported.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-A
Print all five matched parts, tab separated:
.IR bmatch ,
the gap before
.IR want ,
.IR want ,
the gap after it, and
.IR amatch .
.TP
.B \-a
Print three parts, tab separated:
.IR bmatch ", " want " and " amatch .
.TP
.B \-d
Do not insert the default ".*?" gap; require the patterns to match back-to-back.
.TP
.B \-m
Multiline mode: read all of stdin at once, let "." match newlines, and report every match instead of one
per line.
With neither \-A nor \-a, only
.I want
is printed (one per line).

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I bmatch
A regex that must occur before
.IR want .
Must not be empty (use
.BR rpullout (1)
if you don't have a "before" pattern).
.TP
.I want
The regex for the substring you want printed. Must not be empty.
.TP
.I amatch
A regex that must occur after
.IR want .
Optional; defaults to an empty pattern (matches immediately).

.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.B echo 'name: Alice, age: 30' | pullout 'name: ' '\ew+'
.br
Alice
.RE

.RS
.B echo 'a=1 b=2 c=3' | pullout \-a 'b=' '\ed+' ' c'
.br
b=\et2\et c
.RE

.RS
.B nslookup 'example.com' | pullout \-m 'answer' '\eb\ed\eS+'
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including "no lines matched").
.TP
.B 1
.I bmatch
or
.I want
was empty.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (missing arguments).

.SH AUTHOR
Chris Pollitt.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rpullout (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR re (7)
